{
  "what": "PQC geometry — an AUDIT of published SVP-challenge records in exact arithmetic: pi bracketed by Machin, det = q read from the Goldstein-Mayer basis, the acceptance predicate ||v|| <= f*GH raised to the n-th power decided in BigInt. 37 records decided, 0 inconsistent with a true norm that rounds to the printed one, 1 undecidable from the printed norm (dim 119 seed 0). Plus Cohen integral LLL on the dimension-40 challenge basis, 141 snapshots.",
  "charter": "AUDIT ONLY, NEVER DESIGN A PRIMITIVE. CHARTER.md travels with the code and binds every session that touches this folder.",
  "liftedFrom": "/Users/carlostoledo/Documents/frontier-apps/experiments/pqc-geometry",
  "liftedOn": "2026-09-05",
  "declaredPatches": {
    "gh.test.js": "the Python cross-check inserted ../../environments/lattice-claims on sys.path; here the package lives at ../wiring (instruments/wiring/lattice_claims). One path string changed, nothing else."
  },
  "rule": "Copied byte-for-byte and pinned by sha256; frontier-apps has no git. fetch-bases.js talks to latticechallenge.org and is NEVER run by a battery: out/dets.json is the pinned result of the 14 fetches, each determinant proved entry by entry before the basis was discarded. Every other script is offline and deterministic up to wall-clock ms fields; battery.js re-runs them in a scratch copy and compares with ms ignored, so the pinned outputs never churn.",
  "acceptance": {
    "node pi.test.js": "all green",
    "node gh.test.js": "32 cases across 8 real lattices, two implementations, all green",
    "node hof.js": "out/hof.json byte-identical to the pin (926 records)",
    "node audit.js": "37 decided, 0 inconsistent, 1 flip (dim 119 seed 0: ADMISSIBLE at N, REFUSED at N+1/2); identical to the pin up to ms",
    "node reduce.js": "0.22 s; identical to the pin up to ms",
    "node decide-record.js": "exact ratio in [1.049851339, 1.049851340]; 2905 REFUSED",
    "verifiedOn": "2026-09-05"
  },
